  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given NNN distinct points in a 222-D plane, numbered 111 through NNN. The X-coordinate of the points are X1,X2,…,XNX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_NX1​,X2​,…,XN​ respectively and the Y-coordinates are Y1,Y2,…,YNY_1, Y_2, \\ldots, Y_NY1​,Y2​,…,YN​ respectively. Your goal is to make the location of all the NNN points equal to that of each other. To achieve this, you can do some operations.\n\nIn one operation, you choose an index i  (1≤i≤N)i\\;(1 \\leq i \\leq N)i(1≤i≤N) and a **real number** KKK and change the location of the ithi^{th}ith point in one of the following ways:\n\n\nSet (Xi,Yi)=(Xi+K,Yi)(X_i, Y_i) = (X_i + K, Y_i)(Xi​,Yi​)=(Xi​+K,Yi​)\nSet (Xi,Yi)=(Xi,Yi+K)(X_i, Y_i) = (X_i, Y_i + K)(Xi​,Yi​)=(Xi​,Yi​+K)\nSet (Xi,Yi)=(Xi+K,Yi+K)(X_i, Y_i) = (X_i + K, Y_i + K)(Xi​,Yi​)=(Xi​+K,Yi​+K)\nSet (Xi,Yi)=(Xi+K,Yi−K)(X_i, Y_i) = (X_i + K, Y_i - K)(Xi​,Yi​)=(Xi​+K,Yi​−K)\nFind the minimum number of operations to achieve the goal.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach test case contains three lines of input.\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers X1,X2,…,XNX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_NX1​,X2​,…,XN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers Y1,Y2,…,YNY_1, Y_2, \\ldots, Y_NY1​,Y2​,…,YN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer - the minimum number of operations to achieve the goal.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3001 \\leq T \\leq 3001≤T≤300",
      "2≤N≤1002 \\leq N \\leq 1002≤N≤100",
      "−109≤Xi,Yi≤109-10^9 \\leq X_i, Y_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Xi​,Yi​≤109",
      "(Xi,Yi)≠(Xj,Yj)(X_i, Y_i) \\neq (X_j, Y_j)(Xi​,Yi​)=(Xj​,Yj​) if (i≠j)(i \\neq j)(i=j)",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 600600600.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (100 points):** original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n0 1 -4\n0 1 5\n3\n0 1 3\n1 1 -1",
        "output": "3\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111 :\n\n\nIn the first operation, you choose i=2i = 2i=2, and K=−1K = - 1K=−1 and apply the third type of operation. So the location of 2nd2^{nd}2nd point becomes (1−1,1−1)=(0,0)(1 - 1, 1 - 1) = (0, 0)(1−1,1−1)=(0,0).\n\n\nIn the second operation, you choose i=3i = 3i=3, and K=4K = 4K=4 and apply the first type of operation. So the location of 3rd3^{rd}3rd point becomes (−4+4,5)=(0,5)(- 4 + 4, 5) = (0, 5)(−4+4,5)=(0,5).\n\n\nIn the third operation, you choose i=3i = 3i=3, and K=−5K = -5K=−5 and apply the second type of operation. So the location of 3rd3^{rd}3rd point becomes (0,5−5)=(0,0)(0, 5 - 5) = (0, 0)(0,5−5)=(0,0).\n\n\nHence after the above operations, the location of the given three points becomes equal to each other.\nTest case 222 :\n\n\nIn the first operation, you choose i=1i = 1i=1 and K=1K = 1K=1 and apply the first type of operation. So the location of 1st point becomes (0+1,1)=(1,1)(0 + 1, 1) = (1, 1)(0+1,1)=(1,1).\n\n\nIn the second operation, you choose i=3i = 3i=3, and K=−2K = -2K=−2 and apply the fourth type of operation. So the location of 3rd point becomes (3−2,−1−(−2))=(1,1)(3 - 2, -1 - (-2)) = (1, 1)(3−2,−1−(−2))=(1,1).\n\n\nHence after the above operations, the location of the given three points becomes equal to each other."
      }
